  "details": "The text input UI doesn't show clauses indications while inputting Japanese text with IME.\n\nThis movie https://twitter.com/naqtn/status/1558893604067999744 shows typical appearance of Japanese IME (Input Method Editor https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Input_method). Underlines denote how IME currently divides characters into words (\"clauses\") and which part (showing with thick one) is under selecting characters phase. By seeing this, you can choose correct characters (in Kanji notation etc.) For example, see http://nihonshock.com/2010/04/12-japanese-ime-tips/ \"Tip 10: Shift the parsing range\" section.\n\nHowever, The text input UI of VRChat client doesn't show this indications. https://twitter.com/naqtn/status/1558893593657769984 As a result it's harder to input Japanese text properly.\n\nIf I recall correctly, it is a long existing \"bug\". But I think it will be more troublesome on new Chatbox feature.\n\nTested with 2022.2.2p3 build 1222\n\nNote: I used \"clauses indications\" but I don't know what the proper terminology is.\n\n# Short description for Japanese users\nテキスト入力で日本語変換中に文節を示す表示が無いので、正しくするのが困難になっている。おそらく古くからある“バグ”なのだけど、新しい Chatbox 機能においてより問題になりそうだ。",
